WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.190
Hi, welcome back to Gift of Liberation.

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:05.270
And this is Geshe Michael.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:08.210
I'm excited about our course.

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:10.690
It's going to be a very deep course

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.458
and we're going to continue
talking about this idea,

00:00:13.458 --> 00:00:15.240
everybody talks about bodhichitta,

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:19.230
and we hear this word of bodhichitta.

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:22.590
And I think a few people still think

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.740
it means enlightenment mind,

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.520
and then they think it
means the mind of a Buddha

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.190
because bodhi means Buddha
and chitta means mind.

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:33.670
Of course it doesn't mean that.

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:38.240
What it means is the Wish
to reach enlightenment.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:43.240
If we study it for two or three courses,

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:46.630
Lam Rim courses, two or three retreats,

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:51.630
then I think we also start to
forget what is bodhichitta.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:55.070
You can say as the Wish for
enlightenment. That's okay.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:01:00.070
But I very much prefer if you
have the real feeling of it

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:03.220
and the feeling is completely different.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:07.380
It's not to sit and like when you're a kid

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:11.040
and you're wishing for
a bicycle for Christmas.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.290
It's not like that.

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.700
It's not like that. It's
a different kind of thing.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:19.540
So I thought maybe at
the very beginning here

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:23.080
we can do a small meditation,
just a few minutes.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:28.080
You can do a longer one
in your extra classes.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.030
But let's just do a short meditation

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:34.738
on what this bodhichitta feel like.

00:01:34.738 --> 00:01:37.970
And that way we can do the whole course

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:42.050
and we can remember
where we're trying to go.

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:47.050
I will describe the experience
of bodhichitta directly

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:51.650
and then you just follow
along and imagine it.

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:53.110
And I don't know,

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:57.276
when I was in sports when I
played tennis in high school,

00:01:57.276 --> 00:02:01.450
they would tell us to imagine yourself

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:04.280
making these great plays and
doing these great things.

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:08.510
My yoga teacher told me
if you can't do a pose,

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:11.400
then just go halfway into a headstand

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.980
and then imagine yourself
in the headstand.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.930
Then that's a cause for
being able to do it.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:20.160
So we're going to do the
same thing with bodhichitta.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:22.290
So please get ready.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.890
We're going to do just the
little tiny meditation.

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:28.963
You do your serious meditations
in your extra classes.

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:40.493
Eyes are soft. A little bit of a smile.

00:02:44.662 --> 00:02:46.860
Hands are soft. Fingers are soft.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.930
I like to touch my thumbs.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:52.003
I like to put my palms on each other.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.703
Sit up very straight. Shoulders back.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:03.870
I like to...

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:07.910
A strange thing about
pulling in your tummy is

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:12.273
if you exhale two times,

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.370
your stomach will come in automatically.

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:20.220
That's just good for your posture

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.590
and it's good for your health.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:25.278
So let's do long exhales.

00:03:25.278 --> 00:03:26.993
When you run out of breath,

00:03:26.993 --> 00:03:28.497
push a little bit more breath out

00:03:28.497 --> 00:03:31.250
and your lower stomach will tighten

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:32.860
and that will support your back.

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:36.100
Okay, here we go. 10 long exhales.

00:04:55.697 --> 00:04:58.500
And we'll imagine that we're
having the direct experience

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:03.500
of bodhichitta and imagine
your mom comes up in your mind.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:09.150
It's not a picture. It's not a painting.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:10.503
It's not a photograph.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:15.630
It's your real mom, is
in front of your mind.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:20.150
And it's nice to picture her in her health

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:24.890
when you knew her or you saw photos of her

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:28.183
when she was young and healthy, happy.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.665
And you're just sitting together.

00:05:54.318 --> 00:05:56.097
And you're like talking to her,

00:05:56.097 --> 00:05:59.123
"Look, Mom, I know your
life has not been easy.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:05.130
Life is not always easy.
I know you have worries.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:12.680
Wherever you are now, I
know you have more worries.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:14.944
I know you have trouble in your life.

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:21.017
And we have that big fear of death

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:31.503
but I want you to know that
I'm going to take care of you.

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:38.380
It's not an empty
promise. I have the power.

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:42.770
I am learning the power
to take care of you.

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:44.752
You really don't have to worry.

00:06:44.752 --> 00:06:48.490
So kids are supposed to
take care of their parents

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:49.823
when they get older,

00:06:49.823 --> 00:06:54.770
and I've got plans for taking care of you.

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:59.770
I will be a Buddha, a real
Buddha who can go to all places,

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:06.750
all times, all worlds,
and knows all things

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:11.585
and can help you, real help for you.

00:07:11.585 --> 00:07:15.323
I'm on a fast track for that.

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:18.478
So you don't have to worry.

00:07:18.478 --> 00:07:22.880
I know it's my job to take care of you

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:27.022
the way you took care of me
and you don't have to worry.

00:07:27.022 --> 00:07:31.660
I'm on a path and it works.

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:35.250
I can see where it's going and I can see

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:39.627
that I will take care of you ultimately."

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:01.750
And try to picture that day

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:06.750
when you have power to
move from world to world,

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:11.800
planet to planet, galaxy to
galaxy, in countless bodies.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:20.210
It feels like dancing across worlds

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:23.863
and taking care of everyone in each world.

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:27.763
Imagine that power.

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:33.123
Your mind has that power
because your mind is empty.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:37.058
You have that power. You
just have to wake it up.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:48.180
Creating a mandala, perfect world,

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:51.550
perfect universe where no one suffers,

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:53.933
no one gets old, no one dies.

00:08:55.940 --> 00:09:00.213
You have that power. You
are learning how to do it.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:03.392
You are a Buddha in training.

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:07.770
But don't ever forget where you're going

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:11.053
and why we are doing these courses.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.358
Make that promise to your mom.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:26.538
Okay, then you can open your eyes.

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:30.172
Take a stretch me and mom.

00:09:30.172 --> 00:09:32.255
(laughs)

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:39.220
So this course in the Lam Rim,

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:41.840
and we've been going
for almost 10 years now,

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:46.180
over 10 years, and we're
working our way very,

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:51.120
I don't know, for me it's a
great pleasure to come back

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:55.270
to the Lam Rim every few
months in the last 10 years.

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:59.010
For me, it's like swimming in a sauna.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:03.340
I don't know how you call
this heated swimming pool,

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:08.340
or the ocean at San Pacho, or
San Miguel, on very nice day.

00:10:09.794 --> 00:10:14.220
It just feels so pleasant
to come back to the beach

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:17.704
called Lam Rim and jump in the water again

00:10:17.704 --> 00:10:22.704
and kind of get my motivation back,

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:25.800
and get my courage back again,

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:28.639
and then my life doesn't
seem so difficult,

00:10:28.639 --> 00:10:33.600
and I can dream again
about becoming a Buddha.

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:36.700
This book, oh, it's got to be

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:39.160
the greatest book ever written

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:42.360
for the entire Buddhist path.

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:46.786
If you can read Tibetan,

00:10:46.786 --> 00:10:50.593
every single word is extremely beautiful.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:55.440
It makes you think that
Trijang Rinpoche was a special,

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:58.400
very special being, my teacher's teacher.

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:01.790
So you're of a good lineage.

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:03.530
And we're going to continue.

00:11:03.530 --> 00:11:07.053
I'm going to review what
we did in the last Lam Rim,

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:12.530
which was what's the cool stuff

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:16.730
that's going to happen to you
if you can get bodhichitta,

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:21.730
if you can really reach this motivation

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:23.820
and this vision.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:25.020
Never forget the vision.

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:27.700
I don't even like to call it motivation.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:30.770
Get that vision in your mind of traveling

00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:35.770
from planet to planet and
jumping between planets.

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:39.280
It's a lot of fun and you can do it.

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:41.340
Don't think this is the only planet.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:46.100
Come on. Go out and look
at the stars some night.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.850
So keep that in mind.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:52.820
We're going to review
the last Lam Rim we had.

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:57.790
The subject of the last Lam
Rim was really focusing on ten,

00:11:57.790 --> 00:11:59.630
It's called PHAN YON BCU,

00:11:59.630 --> 00:12:02.360
which is the ten benefits of bodhichitta,

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:05.120
the Wish for enlightenment.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:06.870
If you can reach it,

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:08.965
if you can have that direct experience,

00:12:08.965 --> 00:12:10.670
then what's it going to feel like

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:12.910
and how you're going to feel?

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:16.430
So we're going to go
through those ten benefits.

00:12:16.430 --> 00:12:19.600
I'm going to show some IDIMS,

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:23.900
some pictures that give
you a idea of the benefit.

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:27.620
The first one we can show,

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:31.070
so when we talk about the first benefit

00:12:31.070 --> 00:12:35.870
of reaching this kind of vision
of jumping between planets,

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:40.100
dancing between planets,
there are ten benefits.

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:42.010
This is a picture of the first benefit.

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:46.370
I like to call it Visiting
the Middle of the Sun.

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:48.687
And this is called

00:12:48.687 --> 00:12:51.712
THEG CHEN GYI 'JUG SGO SEMS
BSKYED KHO NAR BSTAN PA

00:12:51.712 --> 00:12:55.780
It means you will enter the greater way,

00:12:55.780 --> 00:12:58.760
and it's like going to
the middle of the sun.

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:00.330
Why do I say middle of the sun?

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:03.683
Because it's a very intense, good karma,

00:13:03.683 --> 00:13:07.020
a very, very high good karma.

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:11.710
The good karma of
imagining yourself dancing

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:15.320
between planets and helping
people is incredible.

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:19.150
Just the good karma of imagining it is...

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:21.425
You can even feel it, right?

00:13:21.425 --> 00:13:26.425
When I first taught this last summer,

00:13:26.716 --> 00:13:29.380
we were talking about the virus

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:32.700
and how could we help to stop the virus?

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:34.730
We were talking about,

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:39.010
if we could send the virus
to the middle of the sun,

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:40.610
then that would be great.

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:44.310
Then it'd be great if
we could send the virus

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:47.980
to be destroyed in the middle of the sun.

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:52.980
And also in between that time,
we had the Medicine Buddha

00:13:53.590 --> 00:13:58.590
retreat and all of us were
doing a lot of dedication,

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:03.620
helping save the life of animals,

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:06.720
thinking of ways to save the environment

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:09.410
with our carbon offset program,

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:14.410
and different ways of
helping life on this planet,

00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:16.840
for example, not eating meat.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:20.277
Then people started to write me,

00:14:20.277 --> 00:14:24.100
"Oh, things are happening.
This karma is working."

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:27.230
I think, I don't know about you guys,

00:14:27.230 --> 00:14:31.030
but in America we are very,
what do you call that?

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:34.560
We don't believe those things.
We were very skeptical.

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:37.627
We're like, "Ah, come on,
don't be superstitious."

00:14:37.627 --> 00:14:40.670
Yeah, we studied the Medicine Buddha.

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:45.310
Yeah, we meditated on saving life.

00:14:45.310 --> 00:14:49.410
Yeah, we made plans to stop pollution

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:53.128
and save the forest. But come on,

00:14:53.128 --> 00:14:55.480
it's not really going to
change things like that.

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:57.720
But suddenly, I don't know about you,

00:14:57.720 --> 00:15:01.370
but I started noticing things happening.

00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:05.953
The vaccination came out.
The vaccination was finished.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:08.870
They used to take 10 years,

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:11.490
20 years, to develop a vaccination.

00:15:11.490 --> 00:15:15.650
And this one was developed
in less than a year.

00:15:15.650 --> 00:15:17.160
And then they started giving it

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:20.360
and I actually didn't call anybody.

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:23.130
I didn't plan to get a vaccination.

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:25.970
Just some friends called
me, "Oh, go there.

00:15:25.970 --> 00:15:27.783
They're going to give you a vaccination."

00:15:27.783 --> 00:15:30.540
I went there and I got my vaccination.

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:32.360
Veronica got a vaccination.

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:35.583
Jigme got a vaccination,
first and second one.

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:41.580
Now suddenly, yesterday
we went to a restaurant

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:44.290
for the first time and
we had such a good time

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:47.850
not wearing masks.

00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:49.160
It was so pleasant.

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:53.610
Yhen suddenly things started happening.

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:56.073
McDonald's announced...

00:15:56.073 --> 00:15:59.670
I was looking for a recipe
to cook something at home

00:15:59.670 --> 00:16:01.480
because Veronica is a very good cook

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:06.030
and Geshe Michael is an okay
cook but not like Veronica.

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:09.500
And I thought, "Oh, I want
to learn some new recipes."

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:11.536
I was looking for vegetarian food

00:16:11.536 --> 00:16:16.420
and I found an advertisement
from McDonald's.

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:21.420
They are making a vegetarian
meat, plant-based meat.

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:27.220
And it's a big, big thing now

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:29.290
in Asia, in Singapore, for example.

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:33.030
You can get your Chicken
McNuggets are made from plants.

00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:35.380
This guy was so cute.

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:37.480
He said, "Okay, I'm going to cook some.

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:39.710
I bought some uncooked

00:16:39.710 --> 00:16:40.920
and we're going to cook them together."

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:43.860
I was watching the cook's video

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:48.860
and he cooked this non-meat chicken,

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:50.900
and then he showed how to cook it,

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:52.580
and then he tried it.

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:55.077
Then he tried one and when he was like,

00:16:55.077 --> 00:16:58.210
"Oh my God, that tastes so good."

00:16:58.210 --> 00:16:59.990
And I was like, "Yay!"

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:02.600
McDonald's announced they're going to

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:04.790
serve it in McDonald's.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:05.960
And I was so happy.

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:09.680
Then Bill Gates, one of the
wealthiest guys in the world,

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:11.860
he finished a book.

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:14.090
His suggestion in the book is that

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:19.090
all wealthy countries, OECD,
should become plant-based meat,

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:23.440
all of them, and it would
save the environment.

00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:27.280
He had a very great chapter about that.

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:29.650
Then I got an email from Starbucks.

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:34.650
They say, "Come in on Monday.
It's Meatless Monday."

00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:38.140
Starbucks is not serving meat on Mondays,

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:41.470
and you can have lots of tasty
things, vegetarian things.

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:43.100
And I thought, "Oh my God.

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:48.100
When McDonald's and Starbucks
changed to vegetarian,

00:17:49.110 --> 00:17:51.730
it means my karma is working.

00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:56.460
It means this Lam Rim
bodhichitta meditation

00:17:56.460 --> 00:17:57.810
is definitely working.

00:17:57.810 --> 00:18:01.534
So I don't think it's superstitious.

00:18:01.534 --> 00:18:03.020
I think it's real.

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:06.500
I want to encourage you to think

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:09.210
that we created that.

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:14.110
Those Lam Rim guys, and
those Medicine Buddha guys,

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:16.290
we changed McDonald's.

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:20.550
We made the meat industry vegetarian.

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:24.000
We made vegetarian meat. That's so cool.

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:27.940
I want to encourage you to believe in it.

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:32.880
Like don't be so skeptical
and don't be mean.

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:35.540
Don't say, "Ah, that's superstition."

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:37.100
It's not superstition.

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:42.100
I believe us Lam Rim guys,
and us Medicine Buddha guys,

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:47.370
we changed Starbucks, and
we changed McDonald's,

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:51.740
and we changed Bill
Gates with our Lam Rim.

00:18:51.740 --> 00:18:54.120
So congratulations.

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:57.033
When you get to tantra, when
you get to the Diamond Way,

00:18:58.270 --> 00:18:59.920
it's a bad deed not to believe

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:01.440
that you can change something.

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:05.240
It's a bad deed to think you
didn't change McDonald's.

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:08.110
So let's celebrate.

00:19:08.110 --> 00:19:11.210
We changed McDonald's. Congratulations.

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:14.207
Do you know McDonald's
started in Phoenix, Arizona?

00:19:14.207 --> 00:19:18.410
The first McDonald's
was next to the library.

00:19:18.410 --> 00:19:21.930
My mom used to take us there.
She would buy us french fries.

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:26.930
That was about 50, 60
years ago. Unbelievable.

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:32.017
I never thought that I would
see a McDonald's hamburger

00:19:32.017 --> 00:19:33.580
that's not hamburger.

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:35.853
Congratulations you guys.

00:19:35.853 --> 00:19:38.444
Second advantage,

00:19:38.444 --> 00:19:41.950
and ere we are reviewing the last Lam Rim.

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:44.660
So my idea for this
first class together is

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:48.627
we're just going to review the
then benefits of bodhichitta.

00:19:48.627 --> 00:19:53.627
The first benefit is you
get this incredible karma

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:56.010
that can change anything.

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:56.843
We can say,

00:19:56.843 --> 00:19:58.509
in Tibetan it's called

00:19:58.509 --> 00:20:01.900
THEG CHEN GYI 'JUG SGO SEMS BSKYED

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:06.610
It's the only way to
get into the Mahayana.

00:20:06.610 --> 00:20:10.020
So forget Mahayana as a
philosophy from ancient India.

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:11.430
Don't think like that.

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:14.340
Mahayana means jumping
from planet to planet.

00:20:14.340 --> 00:20:17.370
And you got there. You are there.

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:19.273
Second one,

00:20:19.273 --> 00:20:21.356
let's look at the Tibetan, Tim

00:20:22.605 --> 00:20:27.293
RGYAL BA'I SRAS ZHES BYA BA'I MING THOB PA

00:20:27.293 --> 00:20:29.792
RGYAL BA'I SRAS means

00:20:29.792 --> 00:20:33.093
daughter or son of the Buddhas.

00:20:33.093 --> 00:20:35.720
MING THOB PA means you get that name.

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:38.795
You get the name and
it's such a sexy name.

00:20:38.795 --> 00:20:41.697
I think...There was a rock'n roll song

00:20:41.697 --> 00:20:43.623
when I was younger called Bodhisattva.

00:20:44.810 --> 00:20:47.870
I didn't know what's a
bodhisattva at that time

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:50.130
but it sounded so nice to me.

00:20:50.130 --> 00:20:52.470
The word sounded so nice to me.

00:20:52.470 --> 00:20:55.440
The song got very popular

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:59.640
and you will get the name Bodhisattva.

00:20:59.640 --> 00:21:04.400
It's like, Tim, you're getting
a degree in the college.

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:07.420
They're giving you a degree.

00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:10.410
It's like, Okay, that's
a Buddha on the left,

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:12.760
and you and me are on the right.

00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:17.036
And Buddha's like, "Oh,
okay, this is your degree.

00:21:17.036 --> 00:21:20.560
Now you have a new name like Dr. Tim."

00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:25.203
Or I don't know, Pau Pachi Ph.D.

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:30.570
But now they're going to
call you Bodhisattva Tim

00:21:30.570 --> 00:21:34.090
or Bodhisattva Pachi, Bodhisattva Gyelse.

00:21:34.090 --> 00:21:35.643
And you got a new name.

00:21:35.643 --> 00:21:37.670
And you get a new degree.

00:21:37.670 --> 00:21:41.200
It's really, really beautiful.

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:46.120
It's so beautiful to know
that you're a bodhisattva.

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:49.577
When you hear people say bodhisattva,

00:21:49.577 --> 00:21:51.375
I think bodhisattvas usually

00:21:51.375 --> 00:21:53.050
don't tell people they're bodhisattvas.

00:21:53.050 --> 00:21:56.703
But when you hear people say
bodhisattva, you're like,

00:21:56.703 --> 00:22:01.000
"Yeah, that's me. They're
talking about me."

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:03.337
And you feel happy. You
just feel really happy.

00:22:03.337 --> 00:22:05.470
"Oh yeah, I got that name.

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:08.440
I have that degree, Bodhisattva Degree."

00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:10.190
That's the second benefit

00:22:10.190 --> 00:22:11.357
Third benefit.

00:22:13.422 --> 00:22:17.322
NYAN RANG RIGS KYI SGO NAS ZIL GYIS NON PA

00:22:18.640 --> 00:22:23.640
This is very, very famous
and much, much described

00:22:24.693 --> 00:22:26.526
in the commentaries.

00:22:26.526 --> 00:22:30.755
NYAN RANG means listener,

00:22:30.755 --> 00:22:32.163
NYAN means listener

00:22:32.163 --> 00:22:35.120
and RANG means RANG SANGS
RGYAS self-made Buddha.

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:39.790
But the point is that
these are very, very deep

00:22:39.790 --> 00:22:44.150
spiritual practitioners
who don't have that vision.

00:22:44.150 --> 00:22:48.139
They don't have that vision of
going from planet to planet.

00:22:48.139 --> 00:22:50.670
But they are very beautiful people

00:22:50.670 --> 00:22:52.780
and their meditation is really great.

00:22:52.780 --> 00:22:57.360
Their morality is perfect.
Their concentration is perfect.

00:22:57.360 --> 00:23:00.480
Everything about them is really amazing.

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:05.480
And I like this picture of...
I had this idea of an ocean.

00:23:06.840 --> 00:23:10.920
I saw this picture and it
reminded me of this idea

00:23:10.920 --> 00:23:15.760
that the birds in the
picture are like arhats.

00:23:15.760 --> 00:23:16.890
They reached nirvana.

00:23:16.890 --> 00:23:21.840
These birds are to me, I like
to think they are listeners

00:23:21.840 --> 00:23:23.540
and self-made buddhas.

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:26.060
It's beautiful to watch them

00:23:26.060 --> 00:23:31.060
especially at sunset over
the ocean. But the sun.

00:23:31.670 --> 00:23:33.400
But the sun.

00:23:33.400 --> 00:23:35.877
You can see the reflection of the sun.

00:23:35.877 --> 00:23:37.720
You cannot see the sun.

00:23:37.720 --> 00:23:40.080
But compared to the sun,

00:23:40.080 --> 00:23:42.190
the beauty of the birds is beautiful

00:23:42.190 --> 00:23:44.010
but it's nothing compared to the sun.

00:23:44.010 --> 00:23:47.360
The whole sun lighting up the whole world

00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:48.630
compared to those birds.

00:23:48.630 --> 00:23:51.890
The birds are beautiful. They are arhats.

00:23:51.890 --> 00:23:53.404
They reached nirvana. They are listeners.

00:23:53.404 --> 00:23:55.253
They are self-made buddhas.

00:23:55.253 --> 00:23:58.686
They are people who
didn't have that vision,

00:23:58.686 --> 00:24:00.320
bodhisattva vision.

00:24:00.320 --> 00:24:03.430
And then sun is that higher vision.

00:24:03.430 --> 00:24:05.500
And you become like the sun.

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:09.270
When you're a bodhisattva and
you have that higher vision,

00:24:09.270 --> 00:24:10.670
you become like the sun.

00:24:10.670 --> 00:24:12.360
It doesn't mean the
birds aren't beautiful.

00:24:12.360 --> 00:24:14.070
They're beautiful.

00:24:14.070 --> 00:24:17.100
In fact, the sun makes
them more beautiful.

00:24:17.100 --> 00:24:19.780
But imagine if you could
be the birds and the sun,

00:24:19.780 --> 00:24:21.510
something like that.

00:24:22.830 --> 00:24:25.529
Fourth benefit is called

00:24:25.529 --> 00:24:29.429
MCHOD PA'I ZHING MCHOG TU 'GYUR BA

00:24:29.429 --> 00:24:32.313
MCHOD PA means to make offerings.

00:24:32.313 --> 00:24:37.313
ZHING means garden, in this case, garden.

00:24:37.440 --> 00:24:42.440
MCHOG TU 'GYUR BA means
you become the highest one.

00:24:43.170 --> 00:24:47.820
You become the highest
garden where people can plant

00:24:47.820 --> 00:24:51.130
a good karma of offering.

00:24:51.130 --> 00:24:54.080
And I imagine, wouldn't it be cool

00:24:54.080 --> 00:24:57.840
if you're really a
bodhisattva and you walk

00:24:57.840 --> 00:25:02.510
into the coffee shop
and you order a coffee.

00:25:02.510 --> 00:25:04.580
Like you just walk into the coffee...

00:25:04.580 --> 00:25:06.360
we have a coffee shop next to the college.

00:25:06.360 --> 00:25:11.020
I'm thinking of like, this
lady just became bodhisattva.

00:25:11.020 --> 00:25:12.000
She had that vision.

00:25:12.000 --> 00:25:14.560
Nobody knows she's a bodhisattva,

00:25:14.560 --> 00:25:19.560
but she did reach that vision
in her meditation directly.

00:25:20.010 --> 00:25:21.870
She saw the real thing.

00:25:21.870 --> 00:25:26.350
And now this guy is offering
her a coffee and listen,

00:25:26.350 --> 00:25:29.440
that guy offering her the coffee,

00:25:29.440 --> 00:25:33.000
he suddenly makes this
intense, good karma.

00:25:33.000 --> 00:25:37.940
He suddenly gets this
incredible good karma

00:25:37.940 --> 00:25:41.791
because serving you a coffee
and you're bodhisattva.

00:25:41.791 --> 00:25:46.791
So everyone who is sweet to a bodhisattva

00:25:48.570 --> 00:25:50.600
is collecting extraordinary karma.

00:25:50.600 --> 00:25:55.240
And wouldn't it be nice
to be the bodhisattva.

00:25:55.240 --> 00:25:57.780
Every time someone comes close to you

00:25:57.780 --> 00:26:01.070
and smiles at you or helps you in any way,

00:26:01.070 --> 00:26:03.800
and they don't even know that their karma

00:26:03.800 --> 00:26:07.730
is like a million times more,
they don't even know about it.

00:26:07.730 --> 00:26:10.940
But you are making other people happy just

00:26:10.940 --> 00:26:13.810
by drinking their coffee
at their coffee shop.

00:26:13.810 --> 00:26:16.003
That's so cool.

00:26:16.003 --> 00:26:17.311
Fifth benefit.

00:26:17.311 --> 00:26:20.836
TSOGS RGYA CHEN PO BDE BLAG TU RDZOGS PA

00:26:21.820 --> 00:26:26.220
TSOGS here means, some of
you heard the word TSOGS

00:26:26.220 --> 00:26:31.160
for a dharma party and it means
a lots of good things to eat

00:26:31.160 --> 00:26:32.870
and lots of good things to drink.

00:26:32.870 --> 00:26:34.360
That's called a TSOGS.

00:26:34.360 --> 00:26:35.813
Lots of cool offerings.

00:26:35.813 --> 00:26:39.340
RGYA CHEN PO means very big,

00:26:39.340 --> 00:26:43.140
and BDE BLAG TU RDZOGS PA
means you can make good karma

00:26:43.140 --> 00:26:44.240
very, very quickly.

00:26:44.240 --> 00:26:46.930
I was trying to think
of a photograph for this

00:26:46.930 --> 00:26:48.540
and Gyelse, do you remember

00:26:50.220 --> 00:26:54.660
when we first started
Diamond Mountain University,

00:26:54.660 --> 00:26:59.660
the retreat center, then we
were thinking to build roads

00:27:01.504 --> 00:27:04.838
so we could connect retreat cabins.

00:27:04.838 --> 00:27:09.838
So, I don't know, a hundred
people went out in the desert

00:27:10.500 --> 00:27:12.660
and we picked up rocks.

00:27:12.660 --> 00:27:13.520
It was so funny.

00:27:13.520 --> 00:27:18.520
A hundred people walked
about 50 steps in two hours

00:27:20.020 --> 00:27:21.950
and we just pick up a rocks.

00:27:21.950 --> 00:27:25.590
We'd throw them on the side
and we are making a road.

00:27:25.590 --> 00:27:28.610
It was so funny and we worked so hard.

00:27:28.610 --> 00:27:31.873
Oh my god, you guys go to
Diamond Mountain Retreat Center

00:27:31.873 --> 00:27:36.140
now, you're so lucky.
People worked so hard.

00:27:36.140 --> 00:27:40.180
And I remember we said,
"Let's build a road."

00:27:40.180 --> 00:27:42.260
We used to do that in Boy Scouts.

00:27:42.260 --> 00:27:43.120
Let's build a road.

00:27:43.120 --> 00:27:45.340
We would work for like five days

00:27:45.340 --> 00:27:48.540
and build a road for like a hundred yards.

00:27:48.540 --> 00:27:52.330
So then we were all throwing rocks.

00:27:52.330 --> 00:27:54.900
Then later we got more
money. We got more support.

00:27:54.900 --> 00:27:57.848
And here's the picture.

00:27:59.270 --> 00:28:03.150
Yeah. These machines
came to Diamond Mountain.

00:28:03.150 --> 00:28:05.230
This is Diamond Mountain.

00:28:05.230 --> 00:28:08.149
These are the machines that
were paid for by our sponsors.

00:28:08.149 --> 00:28:12.493
And it's difficult. I took this picture.

00:28:14.570 --> 00:28:17.930
The wheel of the machine
is bigger than me.

00:28:17.930 --> 00:28:19.243
It's taller than me.

00:28:21.040 --> 00:28:24.783
You can make a road, I
don't know, in a few hours.

00:28:26.040 --> 00:28:31.035
You can push those big rocks
to the side, and bodhichitta,

00:28:32.360 --> 00:28:37.336
this bodhisattva's heart, the
bodhisattva's mind is like

00:28:37.336 --> 00:28:39.478
those big machines.

00:28:39.478 --> 00:28:41.156
You want to make good karma?

00:28:41.156 --> 00:28:45.140
It's good karma to pick up
rocks at Diamond Mountain

00:28:45.140 --> 00:28:48.480
but it's going to take you a
hundred years to build a road.

00:28:48.480 --> 00:28:51.103
Go get one of those stupid machines.

00:28:52.640 --> 00:28:55.620
The tire is bigger than
me, taller than me,

00:28:55.620 --> 00:29:00.620
and just use it for a couple
of hours and finish the roads.

00:29:00.750 --> 00:29:04.440
The karma of being a
bodhisattva is like that,

00:29:04.440 --> 00:29:07.311
very, very powerful and very efficient.

00:29:07.311 --> 00:29:09.974
Benefit number six.

00:29:09.974 --> 00:29:12.883
SDIG SGRIB MYUR DU SBYANG BA

00:29:16.254 --> 00:29:17.243
That means,

00:29:17.243 --> 00:29:19.450
SDIG SGRIB means obstacles.

00:29:19.450 --> 00:29:23.030
So we all did bad things in our life.

00:29:23.030 --> 00:29:25.920
We still remember. We're still doing them.

00:29:25.920 --> 00:29:27.530
We can't stop ourselves.

00:29:27.530 --> 00:29:29.090
Sometimes we do bad things.

00:29:29.090 --> 00:29:32.900
We hurt people. We do things
we're not supposed to do.

00:29:32.900 --> 00:29:36.630
And then immediately it creates
an obstacle in our life.

00:29:36.630 --> 00:29:39.560
We've been doing that for our whole life,

00:29:39.560 --> 00:29:43.140
many years collecting
obstacles, one by one.

00:29:43.140 --> 00:29:48.140
We can remove them just by
having that bodhisattva vision.

00:29:48.510 --> 00:29:52.260
So let's call bodhichitta:
the vision of a bodhisattva,

00:29:52.260 --> 00:29:55.300
just by imagining going

00:29:55.300 --> 00:29:58.290
from planet to planet, helping people.

00:29:58.290 --> 00:29:59.980
Just thinking about it

00:29:59.980 --> 00:30:02.250
can remove all these obstacles you have

00:30:02.250 --> 00:30:05.320
in your business life, in your health,

00:30:05.320 --> 00:30:09.740
in your relationships,
in your state of mind.

00:30:09.740 --> 00:30:13.690
Just imagining once in a while

00:30:13.690 --> 00:30:15.690
this goal of dancing from planet

00:30:15.690 --> 00:30:20.060
to planet is enough to
remove all those obstacles.

00:30:20.060 --> 00:30:23.600
You can take medicines.
You can go to doctors.

00:30:23.600 --> 00:30:26.163
You can go to marriage counselors.

00:30:27.230 --> 00:30:32.150
You can talk to business
consultants for many years

00:30:33.580 --> 00:30:37.790
and you won't remove the
obstacles like you can

00:30:37.790 --> 00:30:41.490
with a few short bodhichitta meditations.

00:30:41.490 --> 00:30:44.290
It's just very cool. It's very efficient.

00:30:44.290 --> 00:30:46.420
Saves a lot of money also.

00:30:46.420 --> 00:30:49.545
Benefit number seven.

00:30:49.545 --> 00:30:53.106
CI BSAM PA GRUB PA

00:30:53.106 --> 00:30:55.565
CI BSAM PA means whatever you want,

00:30:55.565 --> 00:30:57.413
anything you can think of.

00:30:57.413 --> 00:30:59.930
CI BSAM PA is a nice word.

00:30:59.930 --> 00:31:02.343
It means anything you can think of.

00:31:02.343 --> 00:31:05.813
GRUB PA You can get it,
anything you can think of.

00:31:05.813 --> 00:31:10.813
I love this organic way to
get things in your life.

00:31:12.890 --> 00:31:16.070
I don't worry about money

00:31:16.070 --> 00:31:19.120
and it was never my goal
in my life to be wealthy.

00:31:19.120 --> 00:31:24.120
I thought if I tried I could
be, but it's not my priority.

00:31:25.190 --> 00:31:27.310
It's not something I want.

00:31:27.310 --> 00:31:30.680
But I would like to have a
lot of money. It would be fun.

00:31:30.680 --> 00:31:32.410
I could do so many good things.

00:31:32.410 --> 00:31:33.850
Mr. Binh in Vietnam,

00:31:33.850 --> 00:31:37.260
he just built 400 houses for poor people.

00:31:37.260 --> 00:31:39.040
I think that's so cool.

00:31:39.040 --> 00:31:41.420
I would like to have money like that.

00:31:41.420 --> 00:31:44.580
And I would like to have
a perfect relationship

00:31:44.580 --> 00:31:46.550
at home with my wife.

00:31:46.550 --> 00:31:49.370
I'd like that to be, and
I'd like to be healthy.

00:31:49.370 --> 00:31:52.670
I don't want to be sick.
Those are things I want.

00:31:52.670 --> 00:31:53.940
Those are things I want.

00:31:53.940 --> 00:31:58.940
And the amazing thing is,
just this bodhisattva vision,

00:31:59.010 --> 00:32:01.710
just thinking about it once in a while,

00:32:01.710 --> 00:32:03.850
things start to happen in your life.

00:32:03.850 --> 00:32:08.420
The karma is so intense that
cool stuff starts to happen

00:32:08.420 --> 00:32:11.830
in your life and you start
to build this perfect world

00:32:13.068 --> 00:32:15.000
without thinking about it.

00:32:15.000 --> 00:32:17.000
You're not like, "Oh, I want to get rich."

00:32:17.000 --> 00:32:19.660
Or you're not like, "Oh, I
want to be super healthy."

00:32:19.660 --> 00:32:22.590
But suddenly all these
things are happening to you.

00:32:22.590 --> 00:32:24.280
If you keep coming back to this vision,

00:32:24.280 --> 00:32:28.573
you got a picture for me,
Pachi, City in the Sun.

00:32:31.320 --> 00:32:34.467
I'm thinking this is a
picture of like Shenzhen.

00:32:34.467 --> 00:32:39.467
In a way, this is a beautiful combination.

00:32:40.290 --> 00:32:43.290
I love this city in China

00:32:43.290 --> 00:32:48.290
because they mix these
beautiful buildings with nature.

00:32:48.330 --> 00:32:51.660
And as you walked through the city,

00:32:51.660 --> 00:32:54.020
there's a beautiful balance.

00:32:54.020 --> 00:32:57.400
People need homes to stay
and people need offices.

00:32:57.400 --> 00:32:59.770
So there are these beautiful buildings

00:32:59.770 --> 00:33:03.410
and there's a sensitivity
to the environment.

00:33:03.410 --> 00:33:06.527
And there's a nice mixture

00:33:06.527 --> 00:33:09.500
in that particular city of nature.

00:33:09.500 --> 00:33:13.710
And without thinking, without planning,

00:33:13.710 --> 00:33:18.220
if you just come back to this
vision a few times a day,

00:33:18.220 --> 00:33:23.220
the karma is so intense that
you will start to have beauty

00:33:24.280 --> 00:33:29.280
and physical wealth around
you, that you didn't dream of,

00:33:29.690 --> 00:33:34.491
and beautiful relationships
and things you didn't dream of.

00:33:34.491 --> 00:33:36.024
Number eight

00:33:36.024 --> 00:33:38.132
Benefit number eight

00:33:38.132 --> 00:33:41.717
GNOD PA DANG BAR CHAD KYIS MI TSUGS PA

00:33:41.717 --> 00:33:46.244
GNOD PA means things that
would cause you trouble.

00:33:46.244 --> 00:33:50.193
BAR CHAD means interruption.

00:33:52.020 --> 00:33:57.020
My teacher used to get really
irritated if he was meditating

00:33:57.070 --> 00:34:00.040
and someone would knock
on the door or something.

00:34:00.040 --> 00:34:01.303
That's called BAR CHAD

00:34:01.303 --> 00:34:04.290
BAR CHAD means your
meditation's going really good

00:34:04.290 --> 00:34:05.860
and then somebody knocks on the door.

00:34:05.860 --> 00:34:07.230
That's called BAR CHAD

00:34:07.230 --> 00:34:11.780
So if you have this vision,
a bodhisattva's vision,

00:34:12.960 --> 00:34:16.730
then those BAR CHADs,
okay, you'll be protected.

00:34:16.730 --> 00:34:21.730
I liked the picture--
Pachi, are you ready? --

00:34:22.945 --> 00:34:25.144
of a tank.

00:34:25.144 --> 00:34:27.932
And look, I know it's a military thing.

00:34:27.932 --> 00:34:30.660
I know it's not a nice thing. It's true.

00:34:30.660 --> 00:34:32.147
It's a very bad thing.

00:34:32.147 --> 00:34:36.930
When tanks...still in this world,

00:34:38.140 --> 00:34:43.140
country's power is calculated
by the number of tanks.

00:34:43.240 --> 00:34:48.052
Still, they say this
country has four thousand.

00:34:48.052 --> 00:34:50.226
This country has three thousand.

00:34:50.226 --> 00:34:52.451
This country has a hundred thousand tanks.

00:34:52.451 --> 00:34:55.230
And if you can imagine a war,

00:34:56.390 --> 00:35:00.047
and if you imagine bullets
flying here and there,

00:35:00.047 --> 00:35:01.415
and people getting killed,

00:35:01.415 --> 00:35:05.970
every few yards, every few
meters somebody's dying,

00:35:05.970 --> 00:35:08.883
then there's this guy
relaxing in the tank,

00:35:08.883 --> 00:35:11.216
probably he's having
a cappuccino, I guess.

00:35:11.216 --> 00:35:14.050
And there's bullets and bombs,

00:35:14.050 --> 00:35:17.360
and people dying, and he just relaxing

00:35:17.360 --> 00:35:20.700
in the tank because nothing
can get through the tank.

00:35:20.700 --> 00:35:24.260
And I know in the
movies, they like to show

00:35:24.260 --> 00:35:27.800
Brad Pitt goes out and
hits the tank with his hand

00:35:27.800 --> 00:35:29.230
and it breaks down.

00:35:29.230 --> 00:35:31.280
It's not like that in a real war.

00:35:31.280 --> 00:35:34.535
The tank comes through
and kills everybody.

00:35:34.535 --> 00:35:37.776
The guys in the tank are just relaxing

00:35:37.776 --> 00:35:39.800
and you can't touch them.

00:35:39.800 --> 00:35:44.800
So bodhichitta is like sitting in a tank.

00:35:45.410 --> 00:35:49.380
The whole world can be crazy and insane,

00:35:49.380 --> 00:35:52.180
people can be doing terrible
things to each other,

00:35:52.180 --> 00:35:57.070
and you're just in this bubble
of bodhichitta protection.

00:35:57.070 --> 00:35:59.940
Just things don't happen to you

00:35:59.940 --> 00:36:03.673
like they happen to other
people: disasters, problems,

00:36:04.797 --> 00:36:08.850
all kinds of disturbances
in their life happened.

00:36:08.850 --> 00:36:13.840
And even you feel guilty, "Oh
I am in the bodhichitta bubble

00:36:13.840 --> 00:36:15.220
and other people are not

00:36:15.220 --> 00:36:17.500
and look they're having so much trouble."

00:36:17.500 --> 00:36:22.110
Yesterday, a friend of mine,
her brother committed suicide.

00:36:22.110 --> 00:36:25.940
And I have to see this.
I have to meet her.

00:36:25.940 --> 00:36:28.970
I have to talk to her.

00:36:28.970 --> 00:36:31.600
I feel like, "Oh, just get in the bubble.

00:36:31.600 --> 00:36:33.800
Just get in the tank.

00:36:33.800 --> 00:36:36.350
Just think about
bodhichitta once in a while,

00:36:36.350 --> 00:36:37.940
you will have this.

00:36:37.940 --> 00:36:39.290
You can be protected."

00:36:39.290 --> 00:36:41.780
That's the eighth benefit.

00:36:41.780 --> 00:36:43.380
Ninth benefit.

00:36:43.380 --> 00:36:47.090
SA LAM THAMS CAD MYUR DU RDZOGS PA

00:36:47.090 --> 00:36:48.531
SA LAM

00:36:48.531 --> 00:36:52.150
SA means bodhisattva levels and

00:36:52.150 --> 00:36:54.023
LAM means path.

00:36:54.023 --> 00:36:57.470
THAMS CAD MYUR DU RDZOGS PA means quickly,

00:36:57.470 --> 00:36:59.210
you'll go through all those paths.

00:36:59.210 --> 00:37:04.210
So the spiritual progress
is judged by five paths

00:37:05.750 --> 00:37:08.300
and ten bodhisattva levels.

00:37:08.300 --> 00:37:11.670
It's very hard to get to the first one.

00:37:11.670 --> 00:37:14.290
It's very hard to get to
the first bodhisattva level.

00:37:14.290 --> 00:37:17.300
When you get to the
first bodhisattva level,

00:37:17.300 --> 00:37:19.250
you already saw emptiness directly.

00:37:19.250 --> 00:37:23.128
That's number one. Imagine
what is number ten.

00:37:23.128 --> 00:37:25.760
But if you have bodhichitta,

00:37:25.760 --> 00:37:28.650
it's like you're climbing a mountain

00:37:28.650 --> 00:37:31.930
and you're just at the top,

00:37:31.930 --> 00:37:35.050
right away you're at the
top. No trouble. No work.

00:37:35.050 --> 00:37:36.750
You don't feel tired.

00:37:36.750 --> 00:37:37.883
Just suddenly

00:37:37.883 --> 00:37:42.583
that bodhichitta can take you to the top,

00:37:42.583 --> 00:37:45.980
Without much trouble, without much sweat,

00:37:45.980 --> 00:37:48.195
without much hard work.

00:37:49.350 --> 00:37:51.890
If you just practice that vision

00:37:51.890 --> 00:37:55.620
we talked about the beginning,
then it's automatic.

00:37:55.620 --> 00:37:59.160
You go to the top of the
ten bodhisattva levels.

00:37:59.160 --> 00:38:00.385
Last benefit.

00:38:00.385 --> 00:38:05.340
'GRO BA'I BDE SKYID MA LUS PA BYUNG BA'I

00:38:05.340 --> 00:38:09.947
ZHING SAR 'GYUR BA'O

00:38:09.947 --> 00:38:11.255
'GRO BA'I BDE SKYID

00:38:11.255 --> 00:38:12.321
BDE SKYID

00:38:12.321 --> 00:38:14.155
I have a friend here in Sedona.

00:38:14.155 --> 00:38:16.139
Her name is, they call her Dickie,

00:38:16.139 --> 00:38:18.081
but her real name is BDE SKYID

00:38:18.081 --> 00:38:19.773
BDE SKYID here it is.

00:38:19.773 --> 00:38:24.330
BDE SKYID means super happy. Super happy.

00:38:24.330 --> 00:38:28.071
I'll show a picture.

00:38:28.071 --> 00:38:31.388
This is valley

00:38:32.454 --> 00:38:35.820
and this whole valley I imagined

00:38:35.820 --> 00:38:38.150
there was a river going through there.

00:38:38.150 --> 00:38:39.830
The whole valley is covered

00:38:39.830 --> 00:38:44.830
with nice, beautiful soil,

00:38:44.940 --> 00:38:47.735
fertile soil.

00:38:47.735 --> 00:38:51.260
You put seeds there, it grows.

00:38:51.260 --> 00:38:53.172
There's places like that.

00:38:53.172 --> 00:38:55.150
Not Arizona.

00:38:55.150 --> 00:38:59.550
But there are places
where the soil is so good

00:39:00.570 --> 00:39:04.735
that just everything will
grow there automatically,

00:39:04.735 --> 00:39:08.739
without any work at all.
Things will grow there.

00:39:08.739 --> 00:39:11.223
And oftentimes, it's river soil.

00:39:12.890 --> 00:39:17.440
The tenth benefit of the
vision of the bodhisattva

00:39:17.440 --> 00:39:21.210
is that you become like a valley

00:39:21.210 --> 00:39:24.827
of fertile soil for other people.

00:39:24.827 --> 00:39:27.060
You become like,

00:39:27.060 --> 00:39:30.700
people can plant their crops in you.

00:39:30.700 --> 00:39:33.740
What crops? Their happiness.

00:39:33.740 --> 00:39:37.720
You are like the good soil.

00:39:37.720 --> 00:39:41.378
And just by being around other people,

00:39:41.378 --> 00:39:43.010
they're good karma increases

00:39:43.010 --> 00:39:47.950
and they can plant their
happiness in you, with you.

00:39:47.950 --> 00:39:52.950
You're available. You're nearby
and you give them a chance.

00:39:55.240 --> 00:39:57.120
Somebody says good morning to bodhisattva

00:39:57.120 --> 00:39:59.270
but they're like already
going to be in nirvana

00:39:59.270 --> 00:40:01.080
within ten years.

00:40:01.080 --> 00:40:03.150
It's crazy.

00:40:03.150 --> 00:40:08.150
So it's nice to be the
soil that other people

00:40:08.940 --> 00:40:13.450
can use to grow their crops
that they need to live

00:40:13.450 --> 00:40:14.966
and to be happy.

00:40:14.966 --> 00:40:18.540
It's nice to be the person in the room

00:40:18.540 --> 00:40:21.615
that is a very fertile soil

00:40:21.615 --> 00:40:23.690
for the happiness of other people.

00:40:23.690 --> 00:40:26.910
And needless to say,
when you become a Buddha,

00:40:26.910 --> 00:40:29.593
after you go through bodhichitta,

00:40:29.593 --> 00:40:32.500
with bodhichitta motivation,

00:40:32.500 --> 00:40:33.970
you become a Buddha.

00:40:33.970 --> 00:40:38.300
Then obviously, it's just
cool to be the person

00:40:38.300 --> 00:40:40.620
who makes billions of other people happy.

00:40:40.620 --> 00:40:44.410
In the end, we are not selfish.

00:40:44.410 --> 00:40:45.860
Human beings are not selfish.

00:40:45.860 --> 00:40:48.510
We want to make other people happy.

00:40:48.510 --> 00:40:52.460
It makes us happy when we
make other people happy.

00:40:52.460 --> 00:40:55.810
And we know that. We feel that.

00:40:55.810 --> 00:40:59.150
And a bodhisattva is going to be the one

00:40:59.150 --> 00:41:01.117
who makes everybody else happy.

00:41:01.117 --> 00:41:05.220
Just imagine you're able to throw a party

00:41:05.220 --> 00:41:08.220
for the whole billions of people

00:41:08.220 --> 00:41:10.690
because you have this bodhichitta.

00:41:10.690 --> 00:41:14.933
So that's a review of the last
Lam Rim course that we had.

00:41:16.000 --> 00:41:18.080
That was just a short review

00:41:18.080 --> 00:41:21.187
of what we went through in
the last Lam Rim course.

00:41:21.187 --> 00:41:25.450
Now we're going to start
the actual instructions

00:41:25.450 --> 00:41:27.200
for how to get to this vision.

00:41:27.200 --> 00:41:31.770
There's actually seven steps,
easy steps, we can take.

00:41:31.770 --> 00:41:34.640
And that's going to be
the new Lam Rim course

00:41:34.640 --> 00:41:36.355
that we're starting on now.

00:41:36.355 --> 00:41:39.757
Let's learn the seven steps we can all do

00:41:39.757 --> 00:41:42.400
to get to this vision.

00:41:42.400 --> 00:41:45.265
So I'll see you in the next episode. Yay!

